  "comments": "Coin minted at the Brussels workshop, composed of 75% copper and 25% nickel. The tolerance for the title has been set at 10 thousandths and for the weight at 40 thousandths. This coin was issued in parallel with the <a href=\"https://fr.numista.com/4194\">1 franc harvonneuse</a> and the <a href=\"https://fr.numista.com/4189\">1 franc puddleur</a> in nickel. Their withdrawal was ordered by the Grand-Ducal decree of November 13, 1952.<br /><br />\r\nFirst coin issued after the Second World War. The economic union with Belgium is re-established, and the Luxembourg franc is once again equivalent to the Belgian franc.",
